The gap: a chart, cross or seal started on a far box reaches the bus host's devices and writes into the bus host's working trees. Nothing coordinates that except asking by hand for "trees?". Include the measurements:
- your 3d8f BUILDME resealed 13 tools/base proofs in the Dell tree and broke cc_0's rebase; 4d59's PROVED was refused on working_tree_clean;
- validate reads PROVES from the gate box's main (your flag);
- akiendell has CAIRN_BUS_HOME empty and runs its own local chart device, so the fleet is already running two chart devices;
- Q#93 (bus eviction) and Akien's singleton message are the nearby intentions.

(Captured from the orchestrator's cross-session message, 2026-11-12, verbatim. The orchestrator: "It's a design question for Akien and me." Measured by akienasus_cc_0 the same night: d5a05b6d1752's first chart was refused at validate with proves_keys_match_the_falsifier_clauses because the proof existed only on akienasus; after pushing it and the Dell pulling, the second chart berthed. Each of d5a05b6d1752's chart, BUILDME and PROVEME crossings, run from akienasus, left records in both Dell trees that cc_0 then committed by hand: commons c3c5cfef, 25dc872c.)
